hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-9 : List Word
hyperactive-interaction-in-the-words-of-the-human-superorganism-9 = unlines (cons "The cords of a symbolic nervous system are literal. Greek *neuron* meant sinew, tendon, bowstring. A nervous system is a system of strings under tension. *Tension* comes from *tendere*, to stretch, the same root as *intention* and *extension*. So the nervous system is made of the same stuff, in the words, as intention and as the tool's extension of a person. Defining HCI as the extension of consciousness by tools describes a nerve growing outward: the cane is a sinew the blind person stretches into the ground." nil)
